# Translation / i18n (always)

English-only help for a French (or any supported) speaker is a **product bug**. Do not ship it.

## Stack

- Chrome: `floqr-i18n.js` → `window.FLOQRI18n` (`data-i18n`, `FLOQRI18n.t`)
- Help: `floqr-i18n-help.js` → `window.FLOQRI18nHelp` (patron / serviceMember / venueAdmin titles+bodies)
- Policy: `translation-policy.html` — **ShoutOut** stays **ShoutOut** in every language
- Gate: `node scripts/i18n-coverage-report.js` and `functions/i18n-coverage.test.js`

## Supported languages (all required)

`en`, `de`, `fr`, `es`, `it`, `pt`, `ru`, `el`, `pl`, `nl`, `ar`

## Who must be fully localized

| Audience | Datapoint | Must translate |
|---|---|---|
| Patron | `IsPatron=1` | Search + My Profile chrome, satellite titles, patron `?` / FloqAi help |
| Service member | `IsServiceMember=1` | Work Calendar / role help |
| Venue admin | `IsVenueAdmin=1` (legacy `IsClubAdmin` / `isClubAdmin` alias into this) | Club Admin chrome + venueAdmin help |

Master Admin–only help may stay English until requested; keyed master **tabs** still follow chrome parity.

## Commit / publish gate (mandatory)

Before **every** commit that touches UI or help, and before **every** Pages publish:

1. **Chrome:** every supported lang has `CHROME.*` key-count **===** `CHROME.en` (no silent English fallback).
2. **Help:** every patron / venueAdmin / serviceMember help id in `floqai-help-repository.js` has title+body in `floqr-i18n-help.js` for **every** non-English supported lang (`de fr es it pt ru el pl nl ar`).
3. New English UI string → `data-i18n` / `t(key)` + fill **all** chrome packs in the same change.
4. New/changed English help → update **all** help locale packs in the same change.
5. Cache-bust `floqr-i18n.js` and `floqr-i18n-help.js` `?v=`.
6. Run `node scripts/i18n-coverage-report.js` — must exit 0.

Incomplete packs → **do not publish**.

## Panel bodies (not just tabs)

Patron/admin **panel body** copy (Inbox rules, compose labels, JS-rendered policy lists via `FLOQRI18n.t`) is in scope for chrome packs—not only nav tabs. When localizing a surface, key the visible panel HTML and any `innerHTML`/`textContent` strings in the page app in the same change. Incomplete panel localization with translated tabs is a product bug.

Language is **not** path-based (`/de/`, `/fr/`). It is `profile.uiLanguage` + `localStorage` selection on the same URLs.

## Protected brands (never translate)

ShoutOut, Mingl, BartR, RydR, FloqAi, FloqR, supRstar, SupRstR, DonPapi, Google, Microsoft, Facebook, Stripe, WhatsApp, SMS, OTP.
